xnu 0175: vote the GPU ARC rails as a batch and fix the RCG update order

The vendor's gen7_rpmh votes gfx.lvl, cx.lvl and mx.lvl as one RPMh batch;
a single command per TCS trigger is a different transaction and the RSC
checks the corners. Add a multi-command TCS write, vote the three rails at
the GPU OPP level 0 (gfx/cx 0x1a0, mx 0x1c0) in one trigger, and print the
TCS command status. Fix the RCG sequence to force the root while the config
is written (the vendor's clk_rcg2_enable order): the old order left UPDATE
stuck at 1 and the AHB branch at 0. Drop the unaligned GENERAL_9/10 and the
RBBM_STATUS reads, which hang the bus while the GMU/GX are off. The hub
clock still does not run; the Android capture in docs/MONDIAN_GPU.md shows
the GX rail is PM8350C S2 and is the next thing to enable.

